  "notes": [
    {
      "text": "Matrix has no physical output socket. The conventions say 'Matrix: fed from Main, EQ corrects the room' but never say where the matrix goes. I did not invent one. This needs answering before the plan can be applied.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "'Matrix: fed from Main' is a routing instruction the plan format cannot express -- there is no field for what feeds a matrix. Recorded here so it is not lost.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "Main's EQ ('set for a recordable sound') and Matrix's EQ ('corrects the room') are both stated as intent with no values. The format has no EQ fields and I would be inventing the values anyway.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "The conventions file's own preamble says the real show's Main fans out to three destinations at once (USB, a card slot, and a recorder). The format holds one socket per output, so I recorded the USB pair the '## Output' section states and am flagging the other two as lost.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "Two watch conditions are stated ('Alert if any vocals-category channel is muted', 'Alert if the Main fader moves below -10dB'). The plan format has no place for them.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reverb Send level: the conventions say vocals route to it post-fader but state no level, so level_db is null on all six vocal sends. A reverb send level is a sound-check decision; unity would have been a guess.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "No channel is routed directly to Main. The conventions route channels to busses and busses to Main, and never state a direct channel-to-Main route. On most real shows most channels do feed Main directly, so this is worth confirming -- but the conventions as written do not say it.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "No starting fader positions or mute states are stated anywhere, so fader_db and muted are null throughout.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "OH is patched to AES50-A 17, out of sequence with the other five drum inputs on A 1-5. That is what the input list says, so that is where it is patched.",
      "source": "model"
    },
    {
      "text": "Horns channels have no DCA. The DCAs section lists six DCAs and horns is not among them; the file's preamble confirms this was true of the source show and is deliberate.",
      "source": "model"
    }
  ]
